Maybe I play slower than most, but I've never had a mintown lamp last
through mine's end and a handful of levels through the main dungeon;
definitely never through the quest, much less to the castle.  (Of
course, I also only remember to turn off lamps when I'm in a lit room
maybe 60% of the time, which could well make a difference.)

> post-Castle, you've got no problems with light.
>
> Light is valuable--I've certainly wished up an oil lamp for Astral
> before (poor planning meant I forgot to bring at least an expired one
> to the planes).  But it's nowhere near as valuable as getting early DSM.

Again, I disagree.  Proper discipline means that you won't be in
desperate need of AC; my Valk had -6 AC when she got to the castle,
which although it made me nervous, wasn't insurmountable.  And I was
playing her almost entirely as a combat wombat.  Point is, I *was*
nervous about my AC--which made me play more cautiously, so I never
really had any problems.  I even meleed the four dragons at the back
with no problem (I was careful to open the doors from the side, so that
they never had a chance to use their breath attacks.)  Early DSM (or
other wish benefit) tends to make one feel invulnerable, which
generally leads to making a mistake which proves you're not.

Your mileage may vary; me, I'll take a light source over a wish, 9
times out of 10.  (Of course, if I run into a situation where I really,
really, really need something in order to survive, you can bet your
sweet assets that I'll be first in line at the wish bar...)

